# Anything reproducible from the sources, or specific to the host that built
# them. node_modules matters most: the backend's better-sqlite3 is a native
# module, and a copy compiled on Windows or macOS cannot load inside a Linux
# container.
**/node_modules
**/dist
**/build

# ...except the collector's Gradle distribution. Its Dockerfile copies that in
# rather than building it — see the note there — so it is the one build output
# that has to reach the context.
!scoring-collector/build/install
!scoring-collector/build/install/**
**/coverage
.git
.gradle
.kotlin
.idea
.vscode
backend/.wrangler
frontend/.ionic

# Secrets. backend/.dev.vars holds all of them, the Article Genie's Cloudflare
# token included; Compose passes it into the container at run time and no
# Dockerfile copies it, so excluding it here keeps it out of the build context
# handed to the daemon as well. The entrypoint writes a local one from the
# committed example, so a stray copy of the real file never reaches a layer.
# Both spellings on purpose: `**/.env` is documented to match zero directories
# too, but a secrets exclusion is the wrong place to rely on reading a spec
# correctly, so the root one is named outright as well.
.env
**/.env
backend/.dev.vars
frontend/.env.local
